cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The AI Engineer Interview Register"
message: >-
  If you use this dataset or its findings, please cite it. When you quote a
  question, carry its source row with it — every row records the URL, author and
  evidence tier it came from.
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "4Geeks Academy"
    website: "https://4geeks.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/breatheco-de/ai-engineer-interview-questions"
abstract: >-
  A register of 1,988 AI-engineer interview questions, unified from 2,354
  recorded instances across candidate posts, compiled reports and published
  study banks. Every question keeps the source type it came from, and every
  count in the accompanying report is split by that source rather than summed.
  The central finding is that the three sources disagree: candidate sittings
  emphasise project defense, agent reliability and index choice, while study
  banks emphasise fine-tuning, serving internals and eval catalogs. Company
  names in the data are tags attached by bank authors, not evidence that the
  company asked the question, and no count in this dataset is a probability that
  a question is asked.
keywords:
  - interview questions
  - AI engineering
  - LLM
  - RAG
  - agents
  - hiring
  - dataset
  - evidence grading
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: "2026-09-24"
version: "1.0.0"
